🔬 Research Methodology Template

1. Project Information

- Title:
- Author: Kurt Celvin
- Date / Version:
- Research area:
- Status: Proposed / In Progress / Validated / Published

2. Research Question

State the question, objective, or hypothesis being investigated.

3. Methodology

Describe the research design, procedures, tools, and analytical methods.

4. Evidence & Sources

List references, datasets, source dates, and relevant provenance information.

5. Assumptions & Variables

Document key assumptions, inputs, variables, and measurement units.

6. Results

Report observations and calculated results. Distinguish results from interpretation.

7. Validation & Reproducibility

Document tests, validation procedures, dependencies, and steps needed to reproduce results.

8. Limitations & Uncertainty

Identify data gaps, known errors, alternative explanations, and unresolved questions.

9. AI Assistance & Human Review

Describe material AI assistance, verification performed, and human review.

10. Ethics, Privacy & Licensing

Confirm public-release suitability, privacy safeguards, attribution, and applicable licenses.

11. Conclusion & Next Steps

Summarize findings without overstating evidence. Identify further research needed.

